{
  "info": {
    "name": "mnjz-chat — mobile endpoints",
    "description": "Endpoints added for the mobile app: reports, support tickets, profile, general settings, working hours and basic automation.\n\n## Setup\nOpen the collection **Variables** tab and set `base_url` and `token`.\n\nAuth is **Bearer Token** at collection level, so every request inherits it — no need to add the header per request.\n\n## Response envelope\nEvery endpoint returns the same shape:\n\n| key | when | notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `statusCode` | always | equals the HTTP status |\n| `success` | always | boolean |\n| `message` | always | **may be `null` on success** — declare it nullable |\n| `data` | success only | **absent from every error response** |\n| `errors` | 400 only | keys are field names, values are `string[]` |\n\n## Pagination\nEvery list returns `data.items` and `data.pagination` (`page`, `per_page`, `total`, `last_page`). `items` is `[]` when empty — never `null`. `per_page` is capped at **100**.\n\n## Roles\n| role | what it can do |\n|---|---|\n| `owner` | everything, and only it can delete ratings |\n| `manager` | everything except deleting ratings |\n| `agent` | reads automation and settings but cannot write them, sees no reports, and sees only its own tickets |\n\nRead the caller's role once from `GET /profile` (`data.role`) and use it to show or hide screens, instead of calling an endpoint and getting a 403.\n\n**403 is not a bug**: either the role is not allowed, or the plan does not include the feature. Show `message` as-is — it is already translated.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "https://app.mnjz.net",
      "description": "server url, no trailing slash"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "description": "sanctum token returned by login"
    },
    {
      "key": "lang",
      "value": "ar",
      "description": "Accept-Language — ar or en. Controls the language of messages and of match_criteria / response_type."
    },
    {
      "key": "rating_uuid",
      "value": "",
      "description": "rating uuid — from get customer ratings"
    },
    {
      "key": "reply_uuid",
      "value": "",
      "description": "canned reply uuid — from get canned replies"
    },
    {
      "key": "template_uuid",
      "value": "",
      "description": "approved template uuid — from get general settings → auth_templates"
    },
    {
      "key": "support_ticket_uuid",
      "value": "",
      "description": "support ticket uuid — from get support tickets"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "reports",
      "description": "Owner and manager only. An agent always gets 403.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "get agent performance",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept-Language",
                "value": "{{lang}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/reports/agent-performance?from=2026-01-01&to=2026-01-31",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "reports",
                "agent-performance"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "from",
                  "value": "2026-01-01",
                  "description": "range start, optional"
                },
                {
                  "key": "to",
                  "value": "2026-01-31",
                  "description": "range end, optional"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Who**: owner, manager\n\n**Plan**: requires the `agent_performance` feature, otherwise 403\n\n**Query**: `from` and `to` as `YYYY-MM-DD`, both optional. Without them the range is the **last 30 days**.\n\n`data.metrics.agents[]` holds per agent: `online`, `last_activity_at`, `active_seconds`, `messages_sent`, `tickets_assigned`, `tickets_closed`, `avg_first_response_seconds`, `avg_resolution_seconds`.\n\n`last_activity_at`, `avg_first_response_seconds` and `avg_resolution_seconds` are **nullable** — an agent who did not work in the range returns null."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "get customer ratings",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept-Language",
                "value": "{{lang}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/reports/ratings?page=1&per_page=25",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "reports",
                "ratings"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "rating",
                  "value": "5",
                  "description": "filter by stars, optional",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "search",
                  "value": "",
                  "description": "matches name, phone or comment, optional",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1",
                  "description": "page number"
                },
                {
                  "key": "per_page",
                  "value": "25",
                  "description": "page size, max 100"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Who**: owner, manager\n\n**Query**: `rating` (1-5), `search`, `page`, `per_page` — all optional\n\n`data.summary` is computed over the **whole filtered set**, not the current page, so the average does not change while paging.\n\n`summary.pending` counts contacts who were asked to rate and have not answered yet — they are **not** in `items`.\n\nUse `can_delete` to show or hide the delete button instead of calling delete and getting a 403."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "delete rating",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept-Language",
                "value": "{{lang}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/reports/ratings/{{rating_uuid}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "reports",
                "ratings",
                "{{rating_uuid}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Who**: **owner only** — a manager gets 403\n\n**Plan**: requires the `rating_delete` feature, otherwise 403\n\nReturns 404 when the rating does not exist or belongs to another organization.\n\nA manager can read ratings but not delete them — the bad rating may be about them."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "get activity log",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept-Language",
                "value": "{{lang}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/reports/activity-log?per_page=50",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "reports",
                "activity-log"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "user_id",
                  "value": "",
                  "description": "filter by team member, optional",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "group",
                  "value": "chats",
                  "description": "event group, optional",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "event",
                  "value": "message_sent",
                  "description": "single event, optional",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "from",
                  "value": "2026-09-01",
                  "description": "from date, optional",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "to",
                  "value": "2026-09-14",
                  "description": "to date, optional",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "per_page",
                  "value": "50",
                  "description": "page size, max 100"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Who**: owner, manager\n\n**Plan**: requires the `activity_log` feature, otherwise 403\n\n**Query**: `user_id`, `group`, `event`, `search`, `from`, `to`, `page`, `per_page` — all optional\n\n`data.members` and `data.groups` are returned so the filters can be built without another call.\n\nShow `data.retention_days` to the user: the log is deleted automatically after that many days, so it does not look incomplete for no reason."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "tickets",
      "description": "A ticket here is the state of a conversation, not a separate entity: every contact has one 'latest' ticket carrying its status and assignee.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "get tickets",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept-Language",
                "value": "{{lang}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/tickets?status=open&page=1&per_page=25",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "tickets"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "status",
                  "value": "open",
                  "description": "open or closed, optional"
                },
                {
                  "key": "assigned_to",
                  "value": "unassigned",
                  "description": "user id or 'unassigned', optional",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "search",
                  "value": "",
                  "description": "matches contact name or phone, optional",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1",
                  "description": "page number"
                },
                {
                  "key": "per_page",
                  "value": "25",
                  "description": "page size, max 100"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Who**: everyone — but an **agent sees only its own tickets**, enforced server side with no query needed\n\n**Query**: `status` (`open`/`closed`), `assigned_to`, `search`, `page`, `per_page` — all optional\n\n`assigned_to` takes a user id or the literal **`unassigned`**.\n\n`assigned_to_name` is ready to display without another call. `assigned_seen` tells whether the assignee has opened it yet.\n\nNullable fields: `assigned_to`, `assigned_to_name`, `contact_name`, `last_message_at`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "get tickets summary",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept-Language",
                "value": "{{lang}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/tickets/summary",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "tickets",
                "summary"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Who**: everyone\n\nReturns `open`, `closed` and `unassigned` counters. For an agent they are scoped to its own tickets."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "support tickets",
      "description": "Tickets you open with OUR support team. Not the same as /tickets, which is the state of customer conversations.",
      "item": [
