    {
      "name": "profile",
      "description": "Every user reads and edits their own profile. No role or plan requirement.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "get profile",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept-Language",
                "value": "{{lang}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/profile",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "profile"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Who**: everyone\n\n`data.role` is the **organization role** (`owner`/`manager`/`agent`), not the platform role.\n\nRead it once on app start and use it to show or hide screens.\n\n`verification_enabled` / `is_verified` / `verification_available` mirror the \"Verifications\" tab in the web profile dialog. Hide the option entirely when `verification_available` is false — the Google Authenticator addon is off.\n\nThis is the SETTING. `/verification/send` and `/verification/confirm` perform a verification; they are unrelated."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "update profile",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept-Language",
                "value": "{{lang}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/profile",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "profile"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Who**: everyone\n\n**Required**: `first_name`, `last_name`, `email`\n\n**Optional**: `phone`, `language`\n\nReturns 400 with `errors.email` when the email is already used by another user.\n\nThe response returns the profile after the update.\n\n`verification_enabled` is optional and boolean. Leave it out and the stored value is not touched — it lives in a different tab in the web UI. It is ignored when the Google Authenticator addon is off.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"first_name\": \"Ahmed\",\n  \"last_name\": \"Salah\",\n  \"email\": \"ahmed@example.com\",\n  \"phone\": \"+966501234567\",\n  \"language\": \"ar\",\n  \"verification_enabled\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "update password",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept-Language",
                "value": "{{lang}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/profile/password",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "profile",
                "password"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Who**: everyone\n\n**Required**: `old_password`, `password`, `password_confirmation`\n\n**Rules**: the new password is at least 6 characters and must match the confirmation.\n\nThe old password is verified first; a wrong one returns 400 with `errors.old_password`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"old_password\": \"current-password\",\n  \"password\": \"new-password\",\n  \"password_confirmation\": \"new-password\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "settings",
      "description": "Reading is open to everyone; writing is owner and manager only.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "get general settings",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept-Language",
                "value": "{{lang}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/settings/general",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "settings",
                "general"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Who**: everyone\n\nReturns the settings plus every dropdown list the screen needs, so no extra call is required: `timezones`, `sounds`, `contact_groups` (options for `campaigns.failed_campaign_group`) and `auth_templates` (APPROVED templates only).\n\n`timezones` and `sounds` are `{value, label}` objects, not plain strings. `notifications.tone` is one of `sounds[].value` — a file path such as `/sounds/message-pop-alert.mp3`.\n\n`auth_template` is the current selection or null. It carries `components` — the template structure as Meta stores it (HEADER / BODY / FOOTER / BUTTONS) — so you can draw the preview from this one call. It is always an array, `[]` when the structure is missing. `parameters` are the saved variables, null when they belong to a different template.\n\nOnly the SELECTED template carries `components`; `auth_templates` stays light. You need `GET /list-templates` only to preview a template the user switched to but has not saved yet."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "update general settings",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept-Language",
                "value": "{{lang}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/settings/general",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "settings",
                "general"
